  If you develop a new program, and you want it to be widely known
and useful, the best way to achieve this is to put it under the GNU
General Public License.  To do so, attach the following notices to
the program.  It is safest to attach them to the start of each source
file to most effectively state the exclusion of warranty; and each
file should have a brief notice like this:

    <program> Copyright (C) <year>  <name of author>
